    <td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>
    </td>

<td>
    Tidal mudflats, sheltered bays, estuaries, lagoons, tidal sloughs. Only occasionally enters low-salinity environments. Burrows into sand or mud at low tide, often sheltered with commensal shrimps or worms (Lee et al. 1980). Scatters eggs (Eschmeyer and Herald 1983). </td>

    <td>
      </td>

<td>
 </td>

<td></td>

<td></td>

<td></td>

<td></td>

<td></td>

<td>
Spawning peaks March-June (Eschmeyer and Herald 1983). </td>

<td>
  </td>

<td>
Abundant. </td>

<td>
  </td>

<td></td>

<td></td>


<td>
Invertivore: Adult, Immature</td>


<td>Actively captures small invertebrates from the substrate.</td>

