  </td>

<td>
  </td>

<td>
  </td>

<td></td>

<td></td>


<td>
Invertivore: Adult, Immature</td>


<td></td>

<td></td>

<td>
</td>

<td></td>

<td></td>
    
<td></td>

<td></td>

<td>
    </td>

<td>
</td>

<td></td>

<td></td>

<td>Range includes the Columbia River system in British Columbia, Idaho, Washington, Oregon, and Nevada; and the Harney basin in Oregon (Page and Burr 2011). <br><br>Northern Harney Basin, Oregon; Snake River basin, including Malheur River, Oregon and Idaho; hybrids (<i>C. hubbsi</i> x <i>C. bendirei</i>) exist in the Willamette River and lower Columbia basin, Oregon; probably occurs in the upper Columbia basin in Washington, southern British Columbia, and possibly elsewhere, but further taxonomic study is needed (Markle and Hill 2000).</td>

