<td>
    </td>

<td>
</td>

<td></td>

<td></td>

<td>This circumboreal-Arctic species ranges from the Beaufort Sea to the Strait of Juan de Fuca in the eastern Pacific Ocean, across southern Arctic Canada, and south in the western Atlantic to Cape Cod, Massachusetts. In the western Pacific, the range extends to Japan and Korea, Sea of Okhotsk (Mecklenburg et al. 2002). Five independent stocks likely in the Bering Sea (Naumenko 1996), 4 or 5 stocks are believed to occur off Newfoundland in the Atlantic Ocean (Carscadden 1981, Nakashima 1992). This species is often associated with the polar ice edge.</td>

<td>
</td>

